Tenali Rama and the Greedy Man (Raw Story)

One day, a greedy man went to King Krishnadevaraya and complained that Tenali Rama had stolen his gold coins.

The king, trusting the man, ordered Tenali Rama to return the gold immediately.

Tenali Rama understood that the man was lying and decided to teach him a lesson.

He calmly asked the man, “How many gold coins did you lose?”

The greedy man thought for a moment and then exaggerated the number, hoping to get more gold than he originally claimed.

Tenali Rama smiled and said, “Your Majesty, this man is clearly lying. A truthful person would not change the number of coins.”

The king realized the truth and became angry.

He punished the greedy man for his dishonesty and praised Tenali Rama for his cleverness.

The greedy man left ashamed, learning a hard lesson.

💖 Moral:

Greed leads to loss.
